#: ../../../projections/misc/misc_robinson.rst:22
msgid "Robinson projection"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../projections/misc/misc_robinson.rst:24
msgid ""
"The Robinson projection, presented by the American geographer and "
"cartographer Arthur H. Robinson in 1963, is a modified cylindrical "
"projection that is neither conformal nor equal-area. Central meridian and "
"all parallels are straight lines; other meridians are curved. It uses lookup "
"tables rather than analytic expressions to make the world map \"look\" right "
"[#f1]_. The scale is true along latitudes 38° north and south. The "
"projection was originally developed for use by Rand McNally and is currently "
"used by the National Geographic Society."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../projections/misc/misc_robinson.rst:33
msgid "**n**\\ [*lon0/*]\\ *scale* or **N**\\ [*lon0/*]\\ *width*"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../projections/misc/misc_robinson.rst:35
msgid ""
"The projection is set with **n** or **N**. The central meridian is set with "
"the optional *lon0*, and the figure size is set with *scale* or *width*."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../projections/misc/misc_robinson.rst:39
msgid "Footnotes"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../projections/misc/misc_robinson.rst:40
msgid ""
"Robinson provided a table of y-coordinates for latitudes every 5°. To "
"project values for intermediate latitudes one must interpolate the table. "
"Different interpolants may result in slightly different maps. GMT uses the "
"interpolant selected by the parameter :gmt-term:`GMT_INTERPOLANT` in the gmt."
"conf file."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../projections/misc/misc_robinson.rst:48
msgid ""
"import pygmt\n"
"from pygmt.params import Axis\n"
"\n"
"fig = pygmt.Figure()\n"
"# Use region \"d\" to specify global region (-180/180/-90/90)\n"
"fig.coast(\n"
"    region=\"d\",\n"
"    projection=\"N12c\",\n"
"    frame=Axis(annot=True, tick=True, grid=True),\n"
"    land=\"ivory\",\n"
"    water=\"bisque4\",\n"
")\n"
"fig.show()"
msgstr ""

